    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/sedimentation_upwind1_flux_D_lev: a minimal consuming model binding NLEV=8 at the import edge, writing dq/dt = -D(W*q, wrt: lev) with the falling density q and the layer-centred downward velocity W both declared over [lev]. The compound match must fire through the fixpoint (priority 10, where q: [lev], W: [lev]) and lower to the rule's two-region makearray -- interior [1,7] holding the imported donor-cell difference stencil aggregate, layer 8 holding the no-inflow top stencil. The model follows the grid's EDGE-ARRAY contract at NLEV=8: it supplies the 9-interface (lev_nodes) quadratic-stretch array ze and derives zc = column_cell_center(ze), dz = column_cell_thickness(ze), all spelled with the literal 8 because the edge binding closes NLEV. The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST -- including the grid-derived geometry observeds -- across bindings.",
